### Rationale
Every routing and CTA shape I tried tied the r2 dispatcher within about 1%, so there is nothing to submit. H18 is refuted. The carve-out switch costs nothing, and the 2.2 MB and 6.6 MB floor decomposition is recorded. I'm returning r2's code unchanged as the candidate. It is not a new design, and I don't recommend spending a portal slot on it.

I measured with b200probe `harness_time`, 3 interleaved repeats, on the rented B200. Medians in µs:

| Shape | r2 padded pair | unpadded pair | row128 | pair64 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2.2 MB | 2.56 | 2.58 | 2.56 | 2.59 |
| 6.6 MB | 3.41 | 3.40 | 3.49 | 3.42 |
| 15.8 MB | 4.54 | 4.58 | 4.64 | 4.58 |
